The door closer assembly integrates several mechanical and hydraulic components designed for smooth operation:
a) Arm & Slide Assembly: Main arm, sliding runner, nylon runner, channel, holding plate, and adjustment screw;
b) Body & Drive Assembly: Pinion assembly, piston, top guide nut, seal retaining ring, shaft seal, top & bottom bearing bush, and packing nut;
c) Hydraulic & Spring Assembly: Inner spring, main spring, regulating valve assembly, end plugs, and filling plug.

A lot comprises door closers of the same nominal size, shape, and manufacture batch. Sizing of double sampling plans is strictly enforced depending on lot size:
a) Lot size up to 50: First sample size is 8 (acceptance number 0, rejection number 2); second sample size is 8 (combined acceptance number 1, rejection number 2);
b) Lot size 51 to 90: First sample size 13 (acc 0, rej 2); second sample 13 (combined acc 1, rej 2);
c) Lot size 91 to 150: First sample size 20 (acc 0, rej 3); second sample 20 (combined acc 3, rej 4);
d) Lot size 151 to 280: First sample size 32 (acc 1, rej 4); second sample 32 (combined acc 4, rej 5);
e) Lot size 281 to 500: First sample size 50 (acc 2, rej 5); second sample 50 (combined acc 6, rej 7);
f) Lot size 501 to 1200: First sample size 80 (acc 3, rej 7); second sample 80 (combined acc 8, rej 9);
g) Lot size 1201 to 3200: First sample size 125 (acc 5, rej 9); second sample 125 (combined acc 12, rej 13).

To prevent UV chalking and degradation, surface coatings must conform to specified chemistries based on grade:
a) Polyester (PE): Allowed for Grade 2;
b) Super Durable Polyester (SDP): Allowed for Grades 2, 3, 4, 5, and 2S;
c) Polyvinylidene Fluoride (PVDF): Allowed for Grades 1, 2, 2S, 3, 4, and 5;
d) Fluoroethylene Vinyl Ether (FEVE): Allowed for Grades 1, 2S, 3, 4, and 5.

Closers are classified by power sizes based on leaf width and door weight:
- Size 2: Max leaf width 850 mm, mass 40 kg;
- Size 3: Max leaf width 950 mm, mass 60 kg;
- Size 4: Max leaf width 1100 mm, mass 80 kg;
- Size 5: Max leaf width 1250 mm, mass 100 kg;
- Size 6: Max leaf width 1400 mm, mass 120 kg;
- Size 7: Max leaf width 1600 mm, mass 160 kg.
Note: For door weights exceeding 160 kg, the performance requirements shall be as agreed between the manufacturer and the purchaser.

Establishes a standardized 6-digit classification code defining the exact performance capabilities of the closer:
- Digit 1 (Category of Use): Grade 3 (closes from >=105°), Grade 4 (closes from >=180°);
- Digit 2 (Durability): Grade 5 (50,000 cycles), Grade 6 (100,000 cycles), Grade 7 (200,000 cycles), Grade 8 (500,000 cycles);
- Digit 3 (Power Size): Defined in Table 1 (sizes 2 to 7, or ranges like 2-4);
- Digit 4 (Fire Resistance): Grade 0 (not suitable), Grade 1 (30 min), Grade 2 (60 min), Grade 3 (90 min), Grade 4 (120 min);
- Digit 5 (Safety): Grade 1 (essential safety-in-use requirements);
- Digit 6 (Corrosion Resistance): Grade 1 (24 h), Grade 2 (48 h), Grade 3 (96 h), Grade 4 (240 h salt spray resistance).

Establishes a performance code defining handle capabilities:
- Digit 1 (Category of Use): Grade 1 (Light Duty) up to Grade 4 (High Frequency/Heavy Duty);
- Digit 2 (Durability): Grade 4 (25,000 cycles) to Grade 7 (200,000 cycles of operation);
- Digit 3 (Test Door Mass): No classification (marked as '-');
- Digit 4 (Fire Resistance): Grade 0 (not suitable) up to fire-rated categories;
- Digit 5 (Safety): Grade 1 (essential safety-in-use requirements);
- Digit 6 (Types of Operation): Grade A (Spring assisted), Grade B (Spring loaded), Grade U (Un-sprung).

Standard testing parameter tolerances are strictly defined:
a) Mass in kilograms or grams: ±2 percent;
b) Length in millimetres: ±2 percent.
